  <!--
    Terminal names. msgflow.xsd derives CompositionType from this type, so the
    assertion applies to every composition. For each connection it checks that
    the source terminal is an output terminal of the source node, and that the
    target terminal is an input terminal of the target node, using the terminal
    lists in IBM's MessageFlow.xsd. The string in the assertion is a table, one
    line per node key (the xmi:type prefix, or className#connectorName):
      key|            marker: this node type has a terminal list
      key|in|id       input terminal  "InTerminal.id"
      key|out|id      output terminal "OutTerminal.id"
    A node whose key has no marker is not checked against a list. That covers
    node types with dynamic terminals, node types with no terminals, subflows,
    user-defined nodes and unrecognised xmi:types.
